# MLIR Optimization Log — matmul_256_512_1024
# Started: 2026-02-26 14:10
# Shape: (256x512) @ (512x1024) -> 256x1024, f64
# Hardware: Intel Xeon E5-2680 v4 (Broadwell), AVX2 (4-wide f64), 28 cores, L1=32KB, L2=256KB, L3=35MB
# Kernel: linalg.matmul with tag="operation_0"

---

## Lessons from previous run (matmul_128_256_128):
- Best schedule: forall[16,1] + tile_K[64] + tile_reg[4,8,4] + hoist_C_from_K_inner + vectorize
- f64 on AVX2: 4-wide vectorization
- M-parallel forall better than N-parallel for row-major access
- DO NOT apply tiling/scf canonicalization after vectorize (hurts perf)
- pack_greedily fails without custom lowering pipeline
- interchange hurts B-matrix locality

---

## Phase 0: Baseline & PyTorch Reference

- MLIR baseline: 312.077 ms
- PyTorch baseline: 0.4936 ms
- Gap: ~632x

